bo'lishi kerak", "Chap farzand har doim o'ng farzanddan katta bo'lishi kerak", "Barcha barg tugunlar bir xil darajada bo'lishi kerak", "Ota tugun qiymati har doim farzandlari qiymatidan kichik bo'lishi kerak"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Max-Heap xususiyatiga ko mezon: har bir ota tugunning qiymati o'zining farzand tugunlari qiymatlaridan katta yoki teng bo'lishi shart."}, {"question": "B-daraxt va Ikkilik qidiruv daraxti (BST) o'rtasidagi asosiy farq nimada?", "options": ["B-daraxtda faqat ikkita farzand bo'ladi", "B-daraxt tugunida birdan ortiq kalit va ikkitadan ortiq farzand bo'lishi mumkin", "BST har doim mukammal balanslashgan bo'ladi", "BST tugunida cheksiz ko'p kalit saqlanadi"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "BST tuguni faqat 1 ta kalit va ko'pi bilan 2 ta farzandga ega bo'lsa, B-daraxt tuguni ko'plab kalitlar va 2 dan ortiq farzandlarni saqlashi mumkin."}, {"question": "Ustuvor navbatni (Priority Queue) eng samarali amalga oshirish uchun qaysi tuzilmadan foydalaniladi?", "options": ["Oddiy tartiblangan massiv", "Stek (Stack)", "Binar uyum (Binary Heap)", "Bir yo'nalishli ro'yxat (Singly Linked List)"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Binar uyum ustuvor navbat uchun eng samarali tuzilma hisoblanadi, chunki element qo'shish va eng yuqori ustuvorlikdagi elementni olish O(log n) vaqt oladi."}, {"question": "Binar uyum (Binary Heap) qanday maвЂ™lumotlar tuzilmasi hisoblanadi?", "options": ["Chiziqli bog'langan ro'yxat", "Kalit-qiymat ko'rinishidagi xesh-jadval", "Muvozanatlanmagan darak-daraxt", "To'liq ikkilik daraxt (Complete Binary Tree) shaklidagi tuzilma"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Binar uyum bu mos ravishda massivda joylashtiriladigan to'liq ikkilik daraxt ko'rinishidagi ma'lumotlar tuzilmasidir."}, {"question": "B-daraxt tartibi t=3 bo'lsa, tugunda maksimal nechta farzand bo'lishi mumkin?", "options": ["5 ta", "6 ta", "9 ta", "3 ta"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "B-daraxtda minimal daraja (tartib) t bo'lganda, tugun maksimal 2t ta farzandga ega bo'lishi mumkin. t=3 bo'lganda 2 * 3 = 6 ta farzand bo'ladi."}]}jЉџf   r_index": 1, "explanation": "\"While\" introduces a longer action in the Past Continuous tense. For \"he,\" the auxiliary verb is \"was.\""}, {"question": "What ___ you doing when I called you yesterday?", "options": ["are", "did", "was", "were"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "This asks about an action in progress in the past, interrupted by another past action. The Past Continuous tense is formed with \"was/were\" + verb-ing. For \"you,\" \"were\" is used."}, {"question": "They were playing football when it ___ to rain.", "options": ["was starting", "started", "had started", "starts"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "\"When\" introduces a shorter, interrupting action in the Past Simple tense that occurs during a longer action in the Past Continuous."}, {"question": "My mother ___ dinner at the moment.", "options": ["cooked", "cooks", "has cooked", "is cooking"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"At the moment\" indicates an action happening now, requiring the Present Continuous tense. For \"my mother\" (she), the auxiliary verb is \"is.\""}, {"question": "The supermarket is ___ close as the bakery.", "options": ["too", "more", "as", "less"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "\"As...as\" is used to show that two things are equal in some way."}, {"question": "When he was young, he ___ run very fast.", "options": ["will be able to", "may", "could", "can"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "\"When he was young\" indicates a past ability, so \"could\" is the correct modal verb."}, {"question": "They ___ coffee every morning.", "options": ["drink", "drank", "drinks", "are drinking"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "\"Every morning\" indicates a regular routine, requiring the Present Simple tense. For \"they,\" the base form of the verb is used."}, {"question": "Water ___ at 100 degrees Celsius.", "options": ["will boil", "boiled", "is boiling", "boils"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "This is a scientific fact, requiring the Present Simple tense. For \"water\" (it), the verb takes an \"-s.\""}, {"question": "This phone is ___ expensive as that one. They cost the same.", "options": ["more", "too", "less", "as"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"As...as\" is used to show that two things are equal in some way. \"They cost the same\" confirms equality."}, {"question": "I'm sorry, I ___ hear you right now.", "options": ["won't be able to", "couldn't", "can't", "might not"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "\"Right now\" indicates a present inability, so \"can't\" is the correct modal verb."}, {"question": "Your cat is ___ beautiful as mine.", "options": ["too", "more", "less", "as"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"As...as\" is used to show that two things are equal in some way."}, {"question": "___ you listen to music every night?", "options": ["Do", "Are", "Did", "Have"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "\"Every night\" indicates a regular habit, requiring the Present Simple tense. For questions in Present Simple with \"you,\" the auxiliary verb is \"Do.\""}, {"question": "My bedroom is ___ big as your bedroom. They are exactly the same size.", "options": ["too", "more", "less", "as"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"As...as\" is used to show that two things are equal in some way. \"They are exactly the same size\" confirms equality."}, {"question": "___ you help me with this heavy bag, please?", "options": ["Can", "Could", "May", "Will"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "\"Could\" is often used for polite requests. \"Can\" is also possible but less formal."}, {"question": "Why ___ you crying now?", "options": ["were", "are", "do", "did"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "\"Now\" indicates an action happening at the moment of speaking, requiring the Present Continuous tense. The auxiliary verb for \"you\" in Present Continuous is \"are.\""}, {"question": "One day, humans ___ live on 