gan yoki ko'rib chiqilayotgan nuqtalar to'plamini bildiradi."}, {"question": "B-daraxt va Ikkilik qidiruv daraxti (BST) o'rtasidagi asosiy farq nimada?", "options": ["B-daraxt faqat ildizga ega, BST faqat barglarga ega", "B-daraxt har bir tugunda bir nechta kalit saqlaydi, BST faqat bitta kalit saqlaydi", "B-daraxt faqat xotirada ishlaydi, BST faqat diskda ishlaydi", "B-daraxt faqat raqamlarni saqlaydi, BST faqat harflarni saqlaydi"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "B-daraxtlar diskda saqlanadigan katta ma'lumotlar bazalari uchun optimallashtirilgan bo'lib, har bir tugunda bir nechta kalit va farzand bo'lishi mumkin. BST esa odatda xotirada saqlanadi va har bir tugunda faqat bitta kalit va maksimal ikkita farzand bo'ladi."}, {"question": "Password Hashing nima uchun ishlatiladi?", "options": ["Parollarni xavfsiz saqlash uchun", "Parollarni shifrlash uchun", "Parollarni tezroq qidirish uchun", "Parollarni tiklash uchun"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Parol xeshlash parollarni to'g'ridan-to'g'ri saqlash o'rniga ularning xesh qiymatlarini saqlash orqali xavfsizlikni oshirish uchun ishlatiladi."}, {"question": "Quyidagi algoritmlardan qaysi biri kriptografik xesh algoritm hisoblanadi?", "options": ["Linear Search", "Bubble Sort", "SHA-256", "Binary Search"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "SHA-256 algoritmi kriptografik xesh algoritm hisoblanadi. MD5 va SHA-1 ham shunday, ammo SHA-256 hozirda xavfsizroq."}, {"question": "C++ dagi unordered_map konteynerining asosi qaysi maвЂ™lumotlar tuzilmasiga tayanadi?", "options": ["Bog'langan ro'yxat", "Xesh jadval", "B-daraxt", "Ikkilik qidiruv daraxti"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "`std::unordered_map` konteyneri xesh jadvaliga asoslangan."}, {"question": "Binar uyumda eng katta (Max-Heap bo'lsa) yoki eng kichik (Min-Heap) element har doim qayerda bo'ladi?", "options": ["Oxirgi elementda", "Ildizda", "O'rtada", "Barglarda"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Uyum xususiyatiga ko'ra, eng katta (Max-Heap) yoki eng kichik (Min-Heap) element har doim ildizda (root) joylashgan bo'ladi."}, {"question": "Xesh funksiyaning  Щ vazifasi nima?", "options": ["Ma'lumotlarni siqish", "Ma'lumotlarni shifrlash", "Ma'lumotlarni tartiblash", "Kalitni massivdagi indeksga aylantirish"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Xesh funksiya kalitni massivdagi indeksga (xesh kodiga) aylantirish vazifasini bajaradi."}, {"question": "Kolliziyani hal qilish usullaridan biri qaysi?", "options": ["Shifrlash", "Zanjirlash (Chaining)", "Saralash", "Qidirish"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Zanjirlash (Chaining) va Ochiq manzillash (Open Addressing) kolliziyani hal qilishning asosiy usullaridir."}, {"question": "Primitiv (sodda) qidiruv algoritmining eng yomon holatdagi vaqt murakkabligi qanday?", "options": ["O(m*n)", "O(m+n)", "O(n)", "O(log n)"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Primitiv qidiruv algoritmining eng yomon holatdagi vaqt murakkabligi O(m*n) dir, bu yerda n - matn uzunligi, m - naqsh uzunligi."}, {"question": "Hisoblash geometriyasidagi Orientatsiya (ing. Orientation) formulasi natijasi manfiy boвЂlsa nimani bildiradi?", "options": ["Nuqtalar soat strelkasiga qarshi joylashgan", "Nuqtalar soat strelkasi bo'yicha joylashgan", "Nuqtalar kollinear", "Nuqtalar bir-biriga ustma-ust tushadi"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Agar orientatsiya formulasi natijasi manfiy bo'lsa, bu nuqtalar soat strelkasi bo'yicha (clockwise) joylashganligini bildiradi."}, {"question": "Muvozanatlangan ikkilik qidiruv daraxti (Balanced Binary Search Tree) nima uchun kerak?", "options": ["Faqatgina kichik ma'lumotlar to'plamlari uchun", "Qidirish operatsiyalarini tezlashtirish va eng yomon holatda O(log n) murakkablikni ta'minlash uchun", "Xotira hajmini kamaytirish uchun", "Faqatgina elementlarni tartiblash uchun"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Muvozanatlangan BST daraxt balandligini logaritmik darajada saqlash orqali qidirish, qo'shish va o'chirish operatsiyalarining eng yomon holatdagi murakkabligini O(log n) ga tushirish uchun kerak."}, {"question": "Heap-Sort algoritmining o'rtacha va eng yomon holatdagi vaqt murakkabligi qanday?", "options": ["O(n^2)", "O(n)", "O(log n)", "O(n log n)"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Heap-Sort algoritmining o'rtacha va eng yomon holatdagi vaqt murakkabligi O(n log n) dir."}, {"question": "Avalanche Effect tushunchasi nimani anglatadi?", "options": ["Kolliziyalar sonining kamayishi", "Xesh qiymatining doimiy bo'lishi", "Xesh qiymatining tez hisoblanishi", "Kirish ma'lumotidagi kichik o'zgarish xesh qiymatida katta o'zgarishlarga olib kelishi"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Avalanche Effect - bu kriptografik xesh funksiyasining xususiyati bo'lib, kirish ma'lumotlaridagi kichik o'zgarish (masalan, bitta bitni o'zgartirish) chiqish xesh qiymatida sezilarli darajada katta o'zgarishlarga olib kelishini bildiradi."}, {"question": "Hisoblash geometriyasida eng sodda obyekt nima?", "options": ["Chiziq", "Uchburchak", "Nuqta", "Doira"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Hisoblash geometriyasida eng sodda obyekt nuqta (point) hisoblanadi."}, {"question": "Convex Hull nechta nuqtadan iborat? Nuqtalar: (0,0), (1,1), (2,2), (3,3)", "options": ["3", "2", "1", "4"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Berilgan nuqtalar bitta to'g'ri chiziqda yotadi. Convex Hull faqat chekka nuqtalardan iborat bo'ladi, ya'ni (0,0) va (3,3)."}, {"question": "Heap-Sort algoritmi ishlashi uchun qancha qo'shimcha xotira talab qilinadi (Space Complexity)?", "options": ["O(n log n)", "O(log n)", "O(1)", "O(n)"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Heap-Sort joyida (in-place) saralash algoritmi bo'lib, O(1) qo'shimcha xotira talab qiladi."}, {"question": "B-daraxt tartibi t=3 bo'lsa, tugunda maksimal nechta farzand bo'lishi mumkin?", "options": ["4", "6", "5", "3"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "B-daraxtda tartib 't' bo'lsa, har bir tugunda maksimal 2t-1 ta kalit va maksimal 2t ta farzand bo'lishi mumkin. Agar t=3 bo'lsa, maksimal farzandlar soni 2*3 = 6 ga teng bo'ladi."}, {"question": "unordered_set qanday qiymatlarni saqlaydi?", "options": ["Kalit-qiymat juftliklari", "Noyob qiymatlar", "Takrorlanuvchi qiymatlar", "Tartiblangan qiym  Ъatlar"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "`unordered_set` noyob qiymatlarni (kalitlarni) saqlaydi, xuddi `std::set` kabi, lekin xesh jadval asosida."}, {"question": "Double Hashing nima ishlatadi?", "options": ["Faqat bitta xesh funksiya", "Ikki xesh funksiya", "Bog'langan ro'yxatlar", "Massivlar"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Double Hashing ochiq manzillashning bir turi bo'lib, ikkinchi xesh funksiyadan foydalanib, kolliziya yuz berganda keyingi bo'sh joyni topish uchun qadam hajmini aniqlaydi."}, {"question": "Xesh funksiya (Hash Function) ning asosiy vazifasi nima?", "options": ["Ma'lumotlarni tartiblash", "Kalitni massivdagi indeksga aylantirish", "Ma'lumotlarni siqish", "Ma'lumotlarni shifrlash"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Xesh funksiyaning asosiy vazifasi kalitni massivdagi indeksga (xesh qiymatiga) aylantirishdir."}, {"question": "Open Addressing usulining mohiyati nimada?", "options": ["Kolliziya yuz berganda yangi xesh jadval yaratish", "Ma'lumotlarni shifrlash", "Kolliziya yuz berganda xesh jadvalda keyingi bo'sh joyni qidirish", "Har bir indeks uchun bog'langan ro'yxat ishlatish"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Open Addressing (Ochiq manzillash) usulida kolliziya yuz berganda, xesh jadvalda keyingi bo'sh joy topilguncha ketma-ket (yoki boshqa proba ketma-ketligi bo'yicha) qidiriladi."}, {"question": "Antivirus dasturlarida qismiy satrlarni qidirish algoritmlarining asosiy vazifasi nima?", "options": ["Tizim tezligini oshirish", "Fayllarni shifrlash", "Virus signaturalarini aniqlash", "Fayllarni siqish"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Antivirus dasturlarida qismiy satrlarni qidirish algoritmlari virus signaturalarini (ma'lum viruslarga xos kod qismlarini) fayllar ichidan topish uchun ishlatiladi."}, {"question": "Quyidagi usullardan qaysi biri kolliziyani bartaraf etish uchun qoвЂllaniladi?", "options": ["Merge Sort", "Binary Search", "Bubble Sort", "Zanjirlash (Chaining)"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Zanjirlash (Chaining) va Ochiq manzillash (Open Addressing) kolliziyani bartaraf etish uchun qo'llaniladigan asosiy usullardir."}, {"question": "Qismiy satr nima?", "options": ["Boshqa bir katta satrning bir qismi bo'lgan satr", "Bitta belgi", "Faqat raqamlardan iborat satr", "Butun bir satr"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Qismiy satr - bu boshqa bir katta satrning bir qismi bo'lgan satr."}, {"question": "Qismiy satr yana qanday nom bilan ataladi?", "options": ["Naqsh", "Matn", "Asosiy satr", "Belgilar to'plami"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Qismiy satr ko'pincha 'naqsh' (pattern) deb ham ataladi, ayniqsa satrlarni qidirish algoritmlarida."}, {"question": "Matn muharrirlaridagi qaysi funksiya satrlardan qismiy satrlarni qidirishga misol boвЂladi?", "options": ["Sahifani saqlash", "Matnni formatlash", "Qidirish va almashtirish", "Imlo tekshiruvi"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Matn muharrirlaridagi 'Qidirish va almashtirish' (Find and Replace) funksiyasi qismiy satrlarni qidirishga misol bo'ladi."}, {"question": "Hisoblash geometriyasi nima?", "options": ["Faqat 3D modellashtirish", "Geometrik obyektlar bilan bog'liq algoritmlarni o'rganadigan soha", "Faqat nuqtalarni chizish", "Faqat chiziqlar bilan ishlaydigan fan"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Hisoblash geometriyasi - bu geometrik muammolarni hal qilish uchun algoritmlarni o'rganadigan informatika sohasi."}, {"question": "Kesma (Line Segment) nima?", "options": ["Cheksiz uzunlikdagi chiziq", "Ikki nuqta orasidagi to'g'ri chiziqning bir qismi", "Faqat bitta nuqta", "Egri chiziq"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Kesma - bu ikki nuqta orasidagi to'g'ri chiziqning bir qismi."}, {"question": "Quyidagilardan qaysi biri xesh funksiyaga misol boвЂladi?", "options": ["sqrt()", "sum()", "key % size", "len()"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Modulus operatori (qoldiqni olish) xesh funksiyalarda kalitni jadval o'lchamiga mos indeksga aylantirish uchun keng qo'llaniladi."}, {"question": "Xesh jadvalda maвЂ™lumotlar nima orqali saqlanadi?", "options": ["Bog'langan ro'yxatlar", "Faqat qiym  Ыatlar", "Faqat indekslar", "Kalit-qiymat juftliklari"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Xesh jadvalda ma'lumotlar kalit-qiymat juftliklari (key-value pairs) orqali saqlanadi, bu yerda kalit xesh funksiya yordamida indeksga aylantiriladi."}, {"question": "Quyidagi tuzilmalardan qaysi biri ichki ravishda xesh funksiyadan foydalanadi?", "options": ["std::list", "std::vector", "std::unordered_map", "std::map"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "`std::unordered_map` va `std::unordered_set` kabi xeshga asoslangan konteynerlar ichki ravishda xesh funksiyadan foydalanadi."}, {"question": "Xesh funksiyalar axborot xavfsizligida nima uchun ishlatiladi?", "options": ["Ma'lumotlarni shifrlash va yaxlitligini tekshirish uchun", "Ma'lumotlarni siqish uchun", "Ma'lumotlarni tartiblash uchun", "Ma'lumotlarni tezroq uzatish uchun"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Xesh funksiyalar axborot xavfsizligida parollarni saqlash, ma'lumotlar yaxlitligini tekshirish, raqamli imzo va boshqa kriptografik maqsadlarda ishlatiladi. Ular ma'lumotni shifrlamaydi, balki uning 'barmoq izini' yaratadi, bu esa yaxlitlikni tekshirishga yordam beradi."}, {"question": "Ustuvor navbatni (Priority Queue) eng samarali amalga oshirish uchun qaysi tuzilmadan foydalaniladi?", "options": ["Massiv", "Xesh jadval", "Bog'langan ro'yxat", "Binar uyum (Heap)"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Ustuvor navbatlar odatda binar uyum (heap) yordamida samarali amalga oshiriladi, chunki u O(log n) vaqt murakkabligida eng katta/kichik elementni olish va qo'shish imkonini beradi."}, {"question": "Quyidagi algoritmlardan qaysi biri hozirgi kunda xavfsiz emas deb hisoblanadi?", "options": ["SHA-256", "MD5", "SHA-3", "Blake2"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "MD5 va SHA-1 algoritmlari kolliziya hujumlariga zaifligi sababli hozirgi kunda xavfsiz emas deb hisoblanadi."}, {"question": "Knut-Morris-Pratt (KMP) algoritmining murakkabligi qaysi javobda keltirilgan?", "options": ["O(log n)", "O(m+n)", "O(n^2)", "O(m*n)"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "KMP algoritmining vaqt murakkabligi O(m+n) dir, bu yerda n - matn uzunligi, m - naqsh uzunligi."}, {"question": "Max-Heap (Maksimal uyum) sharti nima?", "options": ["Ildiz eng kichik element", "Har bir ota tugun o'z bolalaridan katta", "Barcha elementlar tartiblangan", "Har bir ota tugun o'z bolalaridan kichik"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Max-Heapda har bir ota tugun o'z bolalaridan katta yoki teng bo'lishi kerak."}, {"question": "Hisoblash geometriyasi qayerda qoвЂllaniladi?", "options": ["Faqatgina ma'lumotlar bazalarida", "Faqatgina moliyaviy tahlilda", "Kompyuter grafikasi, robototexnika, GIS kabi sohalarda", "Faqatgina matn tahlilida"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Hisoblash geometriyasi kompyuter grafikasi, robototexnika, geografik axborot tizimlari (GIS), CAD/CAM va boshqa ko'plab sohalarda qo'llaniladi."}, {"question": "Hisoblash geometriyasida fazodagi nuqta qanday ifodalanadi?", "options": ["(x, y) koordinatalar juftligi", "(x, y, z) koordinatalar uchligi", "Faqat x koordinata", "Radius va burchak"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Fazodagi nuqta uchta koordinata (x, y, z) bilan ifodalanadi."}, {"question": "Primitiv (sodda) qidiruv algoritmining kamchiligi nima?", "options": ["Juda samarasizligi (eng yomon holatda)", "Faqat kichik satrlar uchun ishlashi", "Juda tez ishlashi", "Juda murakkabligi"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Primitiv qidiruv algoritmi (naive string matching) eng yomon holatda O(m*n) vaqt murakkabligiga ega bo'lib, juda samarasizdir."}, {"question": "Parollarni xeshlashdan asosiy maqsad nima?", "options": ["Parollarni tezroq qidirish", "Parollarni xavfsiz saqlash va ularni ochiq matnda ko'rinmasligini ta'minlash", "Parollarni shifrlash", "Parollarni tiklash"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Parollarni xeshlashdan asosiy maqsad - parollarni to'g'ridan-to'g'ri saqlash o'rniga ularning xesh qiymatlarini saqlash orqali xavfsizlikni oshirish. Agar ma'lumotlar bazasi buzilsa ham, parollar ochiq holda ko'rinmaydi."}, {"question": "Binar uyumda i-indeksdagi tugunn    ing ota tuguni (parent) qaysi formula bilan topiladi?", "options": ["i-1", "2*i + 2", "2*i + 1", "(i-1)/2"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Massivda saqlangan binar uyumda 0-indeksdan boshlansa, 'i' indeksdagi tugunning ota tuguni '(i-1)/2' (butun qismi) formulasi bilan topiladi."}, {"question": "C++ STL da tayyor xesh jadval konteyneri qaysi?", "options": ["std::map", "std::unordered_map", "std::set", "std::vector"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "C++ STL da `std::unordered_map` va `std::unordered_set` xesh jadvallariga asoslangan konteynerlardir."}, {"question": "Agar orientation = 0 boвЂlsa, bu nimani anglatadi?", "options": ["Nuqtalar soat strelkasi bo'yicha joylashgan", "Nuqtalar bir-biriga ustma-ust tushadi", "Nuqtalar soat strelkasiga qarshi joylashgan", "Nuqtalar kollinear"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Orientation 0 bo'lsa, bu uchta nuqta kollinear (bir to'g'ri chiziqda yotadi) degan ma'noni anglatadi."}, {"question": "Kolliziya (Collision) nima?", "options": ["Ikkita kalit bir xil indeksga xeshlanganida", "Ikkita kalit bir xil qiymatga ega bo'lishi", "Xesh jadvalning to'lib ketishi", "Ma'lumotlarning yo'qolishi"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Kolliziya - bu ikki xil kalit xesh funksiya orqali bir xil indeksga (xesh qiymatiga) aylantirilganda yuzaga keladigan holat."}, {"question": "Quyidagi holatlardan qaysi biri hash tableda kolliziya yuz berganini bildiradi?", "options": ["Xesh jadval bo'sh bo'lsa", "Ikki kalit bir xil xesh indeksiga xeshlansa", "Xesh jadval to'la bo'lsa", "Ikki kalit bir xil qiymatga ega bo'lsa"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Kolliziya - bu ikki xil kalit xesh funksiya orqali bir xil indeksga (xesh qiymatiga) aylantirilganda yuzaga keladigan holat."}, {"question": "SHA-256 algoritmi keng qoвЂllaniladigan soha qaysi?", "options": ["Ma'lumotlar bazalari", "Kompyuter grafikasi", "Kriptovalyutalar va raqamli imzo", "Matn tahlili"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "SHA-256 kriptovalyutalar (masalan, Bitcoin), raqamli imzo va ma'lumotlar yaxlitligini tekshirish kabi sohalarda keng qo'llaniladi."}, {"question": "Virus signaturasi deganda nima tushuniladi?", "options": ["Operatsion tizim fayli", "Virusning nomi", "Ma'lum bir virusga xos bo'lgan noyob baytlar ketma-ketligi", "Har qanday dastur kodi"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Virus signaturasi - bu ma'lum bir virusga xos bo'lgan noyob baytlar ketma-ketligi yoki kod qismi bo'lib, antivirus dasturlari uni aniqlash uchun foydalanadi."}, {"question": "Kriptografik xesh funksiyaning asosiy xususiyatlaridan biri qaysi?", "options": ["Bir tomonlama (one-way) bo'lishi", "Tez ishlashi", "Kichik xesh qiymatlarni hosil qilishi", "Ikki tomonlama bo'lishi"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Kriptografik xesh funksiyalar bir tomonlama (one-way) bo'lishi kerak, ya'ni xesh qiymatidan asl ma'lumotni tiklash qiyin bo'lishi kerak."}, {"question": "Satr (ing. String) nima?", "options": ["Belgilar ketma-ketligi", "Tasodifiy belgilar to'plami", "Faqat raqamlar to'plami", "Faqat bitta belgi"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Satr - bu belgilar ketma-ketligi."}, {"question": "Xesh jadvalning oвЂrtacha qidiruv tezligi qanday?", "options": ["O(n log n)", "O(n)", "O(log n)", "O(1)"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Yaxshi xesh funksiya va kolliziyani hal qilish mexanizmi bilan xesh jadvalning o'rtacha qidiruv tezligi O(1) dir."}, {"question": "Nuqta (Point) tekislikda qanday ifodalanadi?", "options": ["Faqat y koordinata", "(x, y) koordinatalar juftligi", "Radius va burchak", "Faqat x koordinata"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Tekislikda nuqta ikki koordinata (x, y) bilan ifodalanadi."}, {"question": "Hisoblash geometriyasidagi qavariq qobiq (Convex Hull) nima?", "options": ["Barcha nuqtalarni o'z ichiga olgan eng kichik qavariq ko'pburchak", "Nuqtalarni birlashtiruvchi chiziq", "Faqat uchta nuqtadan iborat shakl", "Barcha nuqtalarni o'z ichiga olgan eng katta doira"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Qavariq qobiq - bu berilgan nuqtalar to'plamini o'z ichiga olgan eng kichik qavariq ko'pburchak."}]}j›Ђp  Фhun ishlashi"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Primitiv qidiruv algoritmi (naive string matching) eng yomon holatda O(m*n) vaqt murakkabligiga ega bo'lib, juda samarasizdir."}, {"question": "Xesh funksiya (Hash Function) ning asosiy vazifasi nima?", "options": ["Ma'lumotlarni shifrlash", "Ma'lumotlarni siqish", "Kalitni massivdagi indeksga aylantirish", "Ma'lumotlarni tartiblash"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Xesh funksiyaning asosiy vazifasi kalitni massivdagi indeksga (xesh qiymatiga) aylantirishdir."}, {"question": "Orientation (yoвЂnalish) nima aniqlaydi?", "options": ["Uchta nuqtaning bir-biriga nisbatan joylashuvi", "Doiraning radiusi", "Chiziqning uzunligi", "Ikki nuqta orasidagi masofa"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Orientation uchta nuqtaning bir-biriga nisbatan joylashuvini (soat strelkasi bo'yicha, soat strelkasiga qarshi yoki kollinear) aniqlaydi."}, {"question": "Hisoblash geometriyasi qayerda qoвЂllaniladi?", "options": ["Faqatgina moliyaviy tahlilda", "Faqatgina matn tahlilida", "Kompyuter grafikasi, robototexnika, GIS kabi sohalarda", "Faqatgina ma'lumotlar bazalarida"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Hisoblash geometriyasi kompyuter grafikasi, robototexnika, geografik axborot tizimlari (GIS), CAD/CAM va boshqa ko'plab sohalarda qo'llaniladi."}, {"question": "Binar uyumda eng katta (Max-Heap bo'lsa) yoki eng kichik (Min-Heap) element har doim qayerda bo'ladi?", "options": ["Oxirgi elementda", "Ildizda", "O'rtada", "Barglarda"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Uyum xususiyatiga ko'ra, eng katta (Max-Heap) yoki eng kichik (Min-Heap) element har doim ildizda (root) joylashgan bo'ladi."}, {"question": "Kriptografik xesh funksiyaning asosiy xususiyatlaridan biri qaysi?", "options": ["Bir tomonlama (one-way) bo'lishi", "Tez ishlashi", "Kichik xesh qiymatlarni hosil qilishi", "Ikki tomonlama bo'lishi"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Kriptografik xesh funksiyalar bir tomonlama (one-way) bo'lishi kerak, ya'ni xesh qiymatidan asl ma'lumotni tiklash qiyin bo'lishi kerak."}, {"question": "Uyumga yangi element qo'shilganda (Insert), uning o'rnini to'g'rilash jarayoni nima deyiladi?", "options": ["Qidirish", "Heapify-down", "Sortlash", "Sift-up"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Uyumga yangi element qo'shilganda, uyum xususiyatini saqlash uchun element yuqoriga 'ko'tariladi' (sift-up yoki heapify-up) jarayoni amalga oshiriladi."}, {"question": "C++ STL da tayyor xesh jadval konteyneri qaysi?", "options": ["std::unordered_map", "std::set", "std::vector", "std::map"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "C++ STL da `std::unordered_map` va `std::unordered_set` xesh jadvallariga asoslangan konteynerlardir."}, {"question": "Active Set nima?", "options": ["Tasodifiy tanlangan nuqtalar", "Algoritmning joriy bosqichida ko'rib chiqilayotgan nuqtalar to'plami", "Barcha nuqtalar to'plami", "Faqatgina qavariq qobiqni tashkil etuvchi nuqtalar"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Hisoblash geometriyasi kontekstida Active Set ko'pincha algoritmning joriy bosqichida faol ishtirok etayotgan yoki ko'rib chiqilayotgan nuqtalar to'plamini bildiradi."}, {"question": "Quyidagi holatlardan qaysi biri hash tableda kolliziya yuz berganini bildiradi?", "options": ["Ikki kalit bir xil xesh indeksiga xeshlansa", "Xesh jadval bo'sh bo'lsa", "Xesh jadval to'la bo'lsa", "Ikki kalit bir xil qiymatga ega bo'lsa"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Kolliziya - bu ikki xil kalit xesh funksiya orqali bir xil indeksga (xesh qiymatiga) aylantirilganda yuzaga keladigan holat."}, {"question": "Kolliziyani hal qilish usullaridan biri qaysi?", "options": ["Saralash", "Qidirish", "Zanjirlash (Chaining)", "Shifrlash"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Zanjirlash (Chaining) va Ochiq manzillash (Open Addressing) kolliziyani hal qilishning asosiy usullaridir."}, {"question": "Convex Hull nechta nuqtadan iborat? Nuqtalar: (0,0), (3,0), (3,3), (0,3), (1,1), (2,2)", "options": ["4", "3", "6", "5"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Nuqtalar (0,0), (3,0), (3,3), (0,3) kvadrat hosil qiladi. (1,1) va (2,2) nuqtalari e
   Ш Ш                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Ѓєm Q‚уGq_2279c21fb0e74a40b9ec780d81cb4847B{"variant": "B", "quizzes": [{"question": "Convex Hull nechta nuqtadan iborat? Nuqtalar: (0,0), (3,0), (3,3), (0,3), (1,1), (2,2)", "options": ["4", "6", "5", "3"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Nuqtalar (0,0), (3,0), (3,3), (0,3) kvadrat hosil qiladi. (1,1) va (2,2) nuqtalari esa bu kvadratning ichida joylashgan. Shuning uchun Convex Hullni tashkil etuvchi nuqtalar 4 ta bo'ladi: (0,0), (3,0), (3,3), (0,3)."}, {"question": "Binar uyum (Binary Heap) qanday maвЂ™lumotlar tuzilmasi hisoblanadi?", "options": ["To'liq ikkilik daraxt", "Graf", "Chiziqli ro'yxat", "Ikkilik qidiruv daraxti"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Binar uyum - bu to'liq ikkilik daraxt bo'lib, uyum xususiyatini qanoatlantiradi (ota tugun bolalaridan katta/kichik)."}, {"question": "Convex Hull nechta nuqtadan iborat? Nuqtalar: (1,1), (2,2), (3,1), (2,0)", "options": ["4", "3", "2", "1"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Bu nuqtalar romb shaklini hosil qiladi va barcha nuqtalar qavariq qobiqning bir qismi bo'ladi."}, {"question": "Quyidagi nuqtalar toвЂplami uchun Convex Hull nechta nuqtadan iborat boвЂladi? Nuqtalar: (0,0), (2,0), (2,2), (0,2), (1,1)", "options": ["5", "3", "2", "4"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Nuqtalar (0,0), (2,0), (2,2), (0,2) kvadrat hosil qiladi. (1,1) nuqtasi esa bu kvadratning ichida joylashgan. Shuning uchun Convex Hullni tashkil etuvchi nuqtalar 4 ta bo'ladi: (0,0), (2,0), (2,2), (0,2)."}, {"question": "Uyumga yangi element qo'shilganda (Insert), uning o'rnini to'g'rilash jarayoni nima deyiladi?", "options": ["Heapify-down", "Qidirish", "Sift-up", "Sortlash"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Uyumga yangi element qo'shilganda, uyum xususiyatini saqlash uchun element yuqoriga 'ko'tariladi' (sift-up yoki heapify-up) jarayoni amalga oshiriladi."}, {"question": "Binar uyumni massivda saqlashda i-indeksdagi tugunning chap bolasi qaysi formuladan topiladi?", "options": ["2*i + 1", "(i-1)/2", "2*i + 2", "i+1"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Massivda saqlangan binar uyumda 0-indeksdan boshlansa, 'i' indeksdagi tugunning chap bolasi '2*i + 1' formulasi bilan topiladi."}, {"question": "Binar uyumdan ildiz (root) element o'chirilganda, uning o'rniga vaqtincha qaysi element qo'yiladi?", "options": ["Eng kichik element", "Birinchi element", "Oxirgi element", "Eng katta element"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Ildiz element o'chirilganda, uyumning oxirgi elementi ildizga ko'chiriladi va keyin uyum xususiyatini tiklash uchun pastga 'tushiriladi' (heapify-down)."}, {"question": "Qaysi javobda satrdan qismiy satrni qidirishga toвЂgвЂri misol keltirilgan?", "options": ["\"Salom dunyo\" ichidan \"dunyo\" ni qidirish", "\"A\" ichidan \"B\" ni qidirish", "\"123\" ichidan \"456\" ni qidirish", "\"Kitob\" ichidan \"kitob\" ni qidirish"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "\"Salom dunyo\" satridan \"dunyo\" qismiy satrini qidirish - bu satrdan qismiy satrni qidirishning to'g'ri misoli."}, {"question": "Orientation (yoвЂnalish) nima aniqlaydi?", "options": ["Ikki nuqta orasidagi masofa", "Doiraning radiusi", "Chiziqning uzunligi", "Uchta nuqtaning bir-biriga nisbatan joylashuvi"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Orientation uchta nuqtaning bir-biriga nisbatan joylashuvini (soat strelkasi bo'yicha, soat strelkasiga qarshi yoki kollinear) aniqla  Ч  Яt_index": 3, "explanation": "Video conferencing tools are essential for remote workers to communicate and collaborate with colleagues and clients."}, {"question": "Microsoft Azure is a cloud ___.", "options": ["device", "application", "operating system", "platform"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Microsoft Azure is a comprehensive set of cloud services that developers and IT professionals use to build, deploy, and manage applications through a global network of Microsoft-managed data centers. It's a cloud computing platform."}, {"question": "In the UK, drivers ___ drive on the left side of the road.", "options": ["must", "can", "should", "might"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "\"Must\" is used for strong obligations or rules. Driving on the left is a legal requirement in the UK."}, {"question": "Who tests software?", "options": ["Software developers", "Sales representatives", "Project managers", "Quality Assurance (QA) testers"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "QA testers are primarily responsible for identifying bugs and ensuring the quality and functionality of software."}, {"question": "Good UX means easy ___.", "options": ["to use", "to install", "to market", "to code"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "UX (User Experience) focuses on making a product enjoyable and easy for users to interact with."}, {"question": "Why is cybersecurity important?", "options": ["To design websites", "To create new software", "To prevent data theft and damage", "To make computers faster"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Cybersecurity is crucial for protecting sensitive information and critical systems from unauthorized access, damage, or theft."}, {"question": "What are hard skills?", "options": ["Communication skills", "Personal attributes", "Measurable abilities learned through education or training", "Teamwork abilities"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Hard skills are specific, teachable abilities that can be quantified, such as programming, data analysis, or foreign language proficiency."}, {"question": "What are two very polite words to use in emails?", "options": ["LOL and BRB", "Please and Thank you", "ASAP and FYI", "Hey and Yo"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "\"Please\" and \"Thank you\" are fundamental words for showing politeness and respect in written communication."}, {"question": "What is streaming?", "options": ["Downloading files", "Delivering media content over the internet in real-time", "Sending emails", "Storing data on a hard drive"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Streaming allows users to consume media content (audio or video) as it is being delivered, without needing to download the entire file first."}, {"question": "What is telemedicine?", "options": ["A hospital management system", "Remote healthcare services using technology", "A medical device", "A new type of medicine"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Telemedicine involves providing clinical healthcare at a distance using telecommunications technology."}, {"question": "Microsoft Word is ___ software.", "options": ["system", "application", "programming", "utility"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Microsoft Word is an application software used to perform specific tasks, in this case, word processing."}, {"question": "What is teamwork?", "options": ["Collaborative effort of a group to achieve a common goal", "Individual work", "Delegation of tasks", "Competition"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Teamwork involves individuals working together effectively to achieve shared objectives."}, {"question": "What is Git used for?", "options": ["Video editing", "Version control", "Project management", "Graphic design"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Git is a distributed version control system used for tracking changes in source code during software development."}, {"question": "What is hacking?", "options": ["Writing computer code", "Gaining unauthorized access to computer systems", "Playing video games", "Designing websites"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Hacking refers to the act of identifying a  аnd exploiting weaknesses in computer systems or networks to gain unauthorized access."}, {"question": "What does a firewall do?", "options": ["Creates backups", "Speeds up internet connection", "Monitors and controls incoming and outgoing network traffic", "Stores data"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "A firewall acts as a barrier between a trusted internal network and untrusted external networks, controlling traffic based on security rules."}, {"question": "What is ransomware?", "options": ["Malware that encrypts data and demands payment for its release", "A network monitoring tool", "A tool for data recovery", "A type of antivirus software"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Ransomware is a type of malware that encrypts a victim's files, blocking access until a ransom is paid."}, {"question": "What are controllers used for?", "options": ["Listening to music", "Watching movies", "Reading books", "Interacting with games and virtual environments"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Controllers are input devices used to manipulate objects or characters within a game or virtual reality experience."}, {"question": "You ___ eat so much fast food. It's not healthy.", "options": ["don't have to", "couldn't", "mustn't", "shouldn't"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"Shouldn't\" is used to give advice or recommend against an action."}, {"question": "What do startups focus on?", "options": ["Maintaining existing products", "Government contracts", "Innovation and rapid growth", "Large-scale manufacturing"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Startups are typically new companies designed to grow fast by developing unique products or services."}, {"question": "You ___ smoke in the hospital. It's strictly forbidden.", "options": ["shouldn't", "mustn't", "couldn't", "don't have to"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "\"Mustn't\" is used for strict prohibitions, indicating something is not allowed."}, {"question": "What do you wear in VR?", "options": ["Special gloves", "A VR headset", "A full-body suit", "A helmet"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "A VR headset is the primary device worn to experience virtual reality, providing visual and sometimes auditory immersion."}, {"question": "What do freelancers sell?", "options": ["Physical products", "Their skills and services", "Real estate", "Stocks and bonds"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Freelancers are self-employed individuals who offer their professional skills and services to clients on a project-by-project basis."}, {"question": "Software is a computer ___.", "options": ["program", "device", "hardware", "network"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Software refers to the programs and other operating information used by a computer."}, {"question": "What can AI do?", "options": ["All of the above", "Understand language", "Learn", "Solve problems"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "AI systems are designed to perform various tasks that typically require human intelligence, such as learning, problem-solving, and natural language processing."}, {"question": "In a report, what is a 'Blocker'?", "options": ["A type of software", "A project goal", "An obstacle preventing progress", "A team member"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "A blocker is an issue or impediment that prevents a task or project from moving forward."}, {"question": "What can you listen to on Spotify?", "options": ["Video games", "Music and podcasts", "Movies", "E-books"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Spotify is a digital music, podcast, and video service that gives you access to millions of songs and other content from creators all over the world."}, {"question": "What is a startup?", "options": ["A large corporation", "A non-profit organization", "A government agency", "A newly established business"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "A startup is a young company founded by one or more entrepreneurs to develop a unique product or service and bring it to market."}, {"question": "What is a CV?", "options": ["A social media platform", "A document summarizing a person's educ  бation, skills, and experience", "A financial report", "A type of computer virus"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "A CV (Curriculum Vitae) is a detailed document outlining a person's academic and professional history."}, {"question": "What can hackers do?", "options": ["Disrupt services", "Damage systems", "All of the above", "Steal data"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Hackers can engage in various malicious activities, including stealing data, damaging computer systems, and disrupting services."}, {"question": "Who writes code?", "options": ["Project managers", "Software developers", "Graphic designers", "Marketing specialists"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Software developers (or programmers) are responsible for writing, testing, and maintaining the source code of software programs."}, {"question": "What is a Technical Demo?", "options": ["A document outlining technical specifications", "A presentation about project management", "A meeting to discuss technical problems", "A demonstration of a product's technical features and functionality"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "A technical demo showcases the practical application and capabilities of a product or system."}, {"question": "What is entertainment technology?", "options": ["Technology for education", "Technology for business", "Technology used for leisure and amusement", "Technology for healthcare"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Entertainment technology encompasses devices and systems designed to provide enjoyment, such as gaming consoles, streaming services, and VR."}, {"question": "Which of these is a Voice Assistant?", "options": ["Google Chrome", "Microsoft Word", "Siri", "Adobe Photoshop"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Siri is Apple's virtual assistant that uses voice queries and a natural-language user interface to answer questions, make recommendations, and perform actions."}, {"question": "You ___ visit the museum while you are in Paris. It's fantastic!", "options": ["might", "must", "have to", "should"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"Should\" is used to give advice or make a strong recommendation."}, {"question": "I ___ wake up early on weekdays to catch the bus.", "options": ["can", "have to", "should", "might"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "\"Have to\" expresses a necessity or an obligation imposed by an external circumstance."}, {"question": "Who are 'Non-technical' people?", "options": ["IT support staff", "Engineers", "Software developers", "Individuals without specialized knowledge in a technical field"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Non-technical people are those who do not have expertise or a deep understanding of technical subjects."}, {"question": "What is a Project Pitch?", "options": ["A detailed project plan", "A project completion report", "A brief presentation to persuade others about a project idea", "A team meeting agenda"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "A project pitch is a concise and persuasive presentation designed to introduce a project idea and gain support or funding."}, {"question": "What is a 'Milestone'?", "options": ["A significant point or stage in a project", "A type of rock", "A measurement of distance", "A daily task"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "A milestone marks a specific, important point in a project's timeline, often indicating the completion of a major phase or deliverable."}, {"question": "Google Docs is a ___ application.", "options": ["system", "mobile", "cloud-based", "desktop"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Google Docs operates entirely online through a web browser, making it a cloud-based application."}, {"question": "What is data?", "options": ["A type of computer virus", "A programming language", "Facts and statistics collected together for reference or analysis", "A hardware component"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Data refers to raw facts, figures, or information that can be processed or stored by a computer."}, {"question": "He has a bad cold. He ___ stay in bed today.", "options": ["must", "has to", "should", "mig  вht"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "\"Should\" is used to give advice or make a recommendation."}, {"question": "What is spyware?", "options": ["Software that secretly monitors and collects user information", "A type of security camera", "A program for data encryption", "A tool for spying on people"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Spyware is software that enables a user to obtain covert information about another's computer activities by transmitting data covertly from their hard drive."}, {"question": "What is a strong password?", "options": ["A single word", "Long, complex, and unique", "Easy to remember", "Your name or birthday"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "A strong password typically includes a mix of uppercase and lowercase letters, numbers, and symbols, and is not easily guessable."}, {"question": "Which of these is an example of a programming language?", "options": ["Photoshop", "Microsoft Word", "Google Chrome", "Python"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Python is a widely used high-level programming language for general-purpose programming."}, {"question": "Where can you play mobile games?", "options": ["On smart TVs", "On desktop computers", "On gaming consoles", "On smartphones and tablets"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Mobile games are specifically designed to be played on portable devices like smartphones and tablets."}, {"question": "Which of these is an example of system software?", "options": ["Adobe Photoshop", "Operating System", "Google Chrome", "Microsoft Word"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "System software manages and controls 