hat do you wear in VR?", "options": ["A full-body suit", "Special gloves", "A VR headset", "A helmet"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "A VR headset is the primary device worn to experience virtual reality, providing visual and sometimes auditory immersion."}, {"question": "What do PC games use?", "options": ["A VR headset", "A gaming console", "A smartphone", "A computer and monitor"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "PC games are played on personal computers, typically requiring a monitor, keyboard, and mouse."}, {"question": "What is a virus?", "options": ["A network protocol", "A type of computer hardware", "Malicious software that replicates itself and spreads to other computers", "A programming error"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "A computer virus is a type of malicious software that, when executed, replicates itself by modifying other computer programs and inserting its own code."}, {"question": "What can you do in VR?", "options": ["Play games", "All of the above", "Attend virtual meetings", "Explore virtual worlds"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "VR offers a wide range of experiences, from immersive gaming and virtual tourism to educational simulations and collaborative workspaces."}, {"question": "Students ___ bring a dictionary to the exam. It is not allowed.", "options": ["mustn't", "couldn't", "don't have to", "shouldn't"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "\"Mustn't\" indicates a strong prohibition or something that is not allowed."}, {"question": "In the UK, drivers ___ drive on the left side of the road.", "options": ["can", "might", "must", "should"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "\"Must\" is used for strong obligations or rules. Driving on the left is a legal requirement in the UK."}, {"question": "Who tests software?", "options": ["Sales representatives", "Project managers", "Quality Assurance (QA) testers", "Software developers"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "QA testers are primarily responsible for identifying bugs and ensuring the quality and functionality of software."}, {"question": "Remote workers often use a ___.", "options": ["physical office", "video conferencing tool", "time machine", "per  мsonal assistant"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Video conferencing tools are essential for remote workers to communicate and collaborate with colleagues and clients."}, {"question": "You ___ smoke in the hospital. It's strictly forbidden.", "options": ["don't have to", "shouldn't", "couldn't", "mustn't"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"Mustn't\" is used for strict prohibitions, indicating something is not allowed."}, {"question": "Why use antivirus?", "options": ["To browse the internet faster", "To speed up your computer", "To detect and remove malware", "To create documents"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Antivirus software is designed to prevent, detect, and remove malicious software like viruses, worms, and Trojans."}, {"question": "What are soft skills?", "options": ["Project planning", "Technical expertise", "Personal attributes that enable effective interaction", "Financial management"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Soft skills are non-technical skills that relate to how you work and interact with others, such as communication, teamwork, and problem-solving."}, {"question": "User Interface (UI) means how software ___.", "options": ["looks and interacts with users", "stores information", "processes data", "connects to the internet"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "UI refers to the visual elements and interactive properties of a software that users interact with."}, {"question": "Who designs app look?", "options": ["Software developers", "Network engineers", "Database administrators", "UI/UX designers"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "UI (User Interface) designers focus on the visual and interactive elements of an app, determining its look and feel."}, {"question": "What is a Project Pitch?", "options": ["A project completion report", "A team meeting agenda", "A detailed project plan", "A brief presentation to persuade others about a project idea"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "A project pitch is a concise and persuasive presentation designed to introduce a project idea and gain support or funding."}, {"question": "Good UX means easy ___.", "options": ["to code", "to use", "to install", "to market"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "UX (User Experience) focuses on making a product enjoyable and easy for users to interact with."}, {"question": "You ___ pay to enter the park. It is completely free.", "options": ["mustn't", "can't", "shouldn't", "don't have to"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"Don't have to\" indicates that something is not necessary or not an obligation."}, {"question": "What is spyware?", "options": ["Software that secretly monitors and collects user information", "A tool for spying on people", "A type of security camera", "A program for data encryption"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Spyware is software that enables a user to obtain covert information about another's computer activities by transmitting data covertly from their hard drive."}, {"question": "Why is cybersecurity important?", "options": ["To create new software", "To make computers faster", "To design websites", "To prevent data theft and damage"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Cybersecurity is crucial for protecting sensitive information and critical systems from unauthorized access, damage, or theft."}, {"question": "Who writes code?", "options": ["Software developers", "Marketing specialists", "Graphic designers", "Project managers"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Software developers (or programmers) are responsible for writing, testing, and maintaining the source code of software programs."}, {"question": "Children ___ listen to their parents.", "options": ["might", "must", "have to", "should"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"Should\" is used for general advice or what is considered morally correct."}, {"question": "What is Artificial Intelligence?", "options": ["A type of robot", "A new programming language", "Machines that mimic human intelligence", "A computer game"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "AI refers to the simulation of human intell  нigence in machines that are programmed to think like humans and mimic their actions."}, {"question": "Which of these is a Voice Assistant?", "options": ["Microsoft Word", "Google Chrome", "Adobe Photoshop", "Siri"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Siri is Apple's virtual assistant that uses voice queries and a natural-language user interface to answer questions, make recommendations, and perform actions."}, {"question": "What is Git used for?", "options": ["Project management", "Video editing", "Version control", "Graphic design"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Git is a distributed version control system used for tracking changes in source code during software development."}, {"question": "What does 'Proofread' mean?", "options": ["To write a draft", "To read and correct errors in text", "To publish a document", "To summarize a text"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Proofreading involves carefully checking a text for grammatical, spelling, punctuation, and formatting errors before final submission."}, {"question": "What is a strong password?", "options": ["Long, complex, and unique", "Easy to remember", "A single word", "Your name or birthday"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "A strong password typically includes a mix of uppercase and lowercase letters, numbers, and symbols, and is not easily guessable."}, {"question": "What is a 'Chart'?", "options": ["A type of map", "A written document", "A graphical representation of data", "A musical score"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "A chart is a visual display of information, often used to show relationships between different data sets."}, {"question": "When do you write an Incident Report?", "options": ["After