d."}, {"question": "What are controllers used for?", "options": ["Reading books", "Listening to music", "Watching movies", "Interacting with games and virtual environments"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Controllers are input devices used to manipulate objects or characters within a game or virtual reality experience."}, {"question": "What do freelancers sell?", "options":   о["Their skills and services", "Physical products", "Stocks and bonds", "Real estate"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Freelancers are self-employed individuals who offer their professional skills and services to clients on a project-by-project basis."}, {"question": "What does AI learn from?", "options": ["All of the above", "Other AI", "Data", "Human teachers"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "AI systems learn from vast amounts of data, often with human supervision, and can even learn from interactions with other AI or environments."}, {"question": "What is data?", "options": ["A hardware component", "A type of computer virus", "Facts and statistics collected together for reference or analysis", "A programming language"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Data refers to raw facts, figures, or information that can be processed or stored by a computer."}, {"question": "What is telemedicine?", "options": ["A medical device", "A new type of medicine", "A hospital management system", "Remote healthcare services using technology"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Telemedicine involves providing clinical healthcare at a distance using telecommunications technology."}, {"question": "Which sign-off is informal?", "options": ["Cheers", "Sincerely", "Best regards", "Yours faithfully"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "\"Cheers\" is a casual and informal way to sign off an email or message."}, {"question": "Which of these is an example of system software?", "options": ["Microsoft Word", "Adobe Photoshop", "Operating System", "Google Chrome"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "System software manages and controls the computer hardware and provides a platform for application software. An operating system is a prime example."}, {"question": "Who are 'Non-technical' people?", "options": ["IT support staff", "Individuals without specialized knowledge in a technical field", "Engineers", "Software developers"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Non-technical people are those who do not have expertise or a deep understanding of technical subjects."}, {"question": "What is a Progress Report for?", "options": ["To inform stakeholders about the status of a project", "To finalize a project", "To propose a new idea", "To report an incident"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "A progress report provides an update on the status of a project or task, highlighting achievements, challenges, and next steps."}, {"question": "What is a 'Summary'?", "options": ["A list of all facts", "A brief statement of the main points", "A personal opinion", "A detailed analysis"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "A summary provides a concise overview of the key information or main ideas of a longer text or presentation."}, {"question": "What does malware do?", "options": ["Harm computer systems", "Steal information", "Disrupt operations", "All of the above"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Malware is a broad term for any software designed to cause damage, steal data, or disrupt computer operations."}, {"question": "What does K.I.S.S. mean?", "options": ["Keep It Short and Sweet", "Keep It Smart, Simple", "Keep It Secret, Safe", "Keep It Simple, Stupid"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "K.I.S.S. is an acronym for \"Keep It Simple, Stupid,\" a design principle that states that most systems work best if they are kept simple rather than made complicated."}, {"question": "What are hard skills?", "options": ["Personal attributes", "Measurable abilities learned through education or training", "Communication skills", "Teamwork abilities"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Hard skills are specific, teachable abilities that can be quantified, such as programming, data analysis, or foreign language proficiency."}, {"question": "What is a startup?", "options": ["A large corporation", "A government agency", "A newly established business", "A non-profit organization"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "A startup is a young company founded by one or more entrepreneurs to develop a unique product or service and bring it to market."}, {"q    uestion": "What is entertainment technology?", "options": ["Technology for education", "Technology for healthcare", "Technology used for leisure and amusement", "Technology for business"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Entertainment technology encompasses devices and systems designed to provide enjoyment, such as gaming consoles, streaming services, and VR."}, {"question": "He has a bad cold. He ___ stay in bed today.", "options": ["has to", "should", "must", "might"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "\"Should\" is used to give advice or make a recommendation."}, {"question": "What is VR?", "options": ["Virtual Reality", "Voice Recognition", "Video Recording", "Visual Rendering"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "VR stands for Virtual Reality, a simulated experience that can be similar to or completely different from the real world."}, {"question": "Microsoft Word is ___ software.", "options": ["programming", "system", "utility", "application"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Microsoft Word is an application software used to perform specific tasks, in this case, word processing."}, {"question": "Which of these is an example of a programming language?", "options": ["Python", "Photoshop", "Microsoft Word", "Google Chrome"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Python is a widely used high-level programming language for general-purpose programming."}, {"question": "Software is a computer ___.", "options": ["program", "hardware", "network", "device"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Software refers to the programs and other operating information used by a computer."}, {"question": "What is E-sports?", "options": ["A type of exercise", "Competitive video gaming", "Electronic sports equipment", "A new programming language"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "E-sports (electronic sports) refers to organized, multiplayer video game competitions, often between professional players."}, {"question": "What is a 'Milestone'?", "options": ["A measurement of distance", "A type of rock", "A daily task", "A significant point or stage in a project"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "A milestone marks a specific, important point in a project's timeline, often indicating the completion of a major phase or deliverable."}, {"question": "What is teamwork?", "options": ["Collaborative effort of a group to achieve a common goal", "Individual work", "Delegation of tasks", "Competition"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Teamwork involves individuals working together effectively to achieve shared objectives."}, {"question": "What are two very polite words to use in emails?", "options": ["Hey and Yo", "LOL and BRB", "ASAP and FYI", "Please and Thank you"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"Please\" and \"Thank you\" are fundamental words for showing politeness and respect in written communication."}, {"question": "Google Drive is a type of cloud ___.", "options": ["computing", "storage", "networking", "security"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Google Drive is a file storage and synchronization service developed by Google, allowing users to store files on their servers."}, {"question": "What is streaming?", "options": ["Sending emails", "Downloading files", "Storing data on a hard drive", "Delivering media content over the internet in real-time"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Streaming allows users to consume media content (audio or video) as it is being delivered, without needing to download the entire file first."}, {"question": "What 