", "Company profits", "Physical buildings"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Cybersecurity is the practice of protecting systems, networks, and programs from digital attacks."}, {"question": "Who tests software?", "options": ["Quality Assurance (QA) testers", "Sales representatives", "Software developers", "Project managers"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "QA testers are primarily responsible for identifying bugs and ensuring the quality and functionality of software."}, {"question": "What does AI learn from?", "options": ["All of the above", "Data", "Other AI", "Human teachers"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "AI systems learn from vast amounts of data, often with human supervision, and can even learn from interactions with other AI or environments."}, {"question": "What are 'Visual Aids'?", "options": ["Sound effects", "Images, charts, or videos used to enhance a presentation", "Spoken words", "Written notes"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Visual aids are supplementary materials that help an audience understand and retain information, such as slides, diagrams, or objects."}, {"question": "He has a bad cold. He ___ stay in bed today.", "options": ["must", "might", "has to", "should"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"Should\" is used to give advice or make a recommendation."}, {"question": "You ___ visit the museum while you are in Paris. It's fantastic!", "options": ["should", "have to", "might", "must"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "\"Should\" is used to give advice or make a strong recommendation."}, {"question": "What is telemedicine?", "options": ["Remote healthcare services using technology", "A hospital management system", "A new type of medicine", "A medical device"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Telemedicine involves providing clinical healthcare at a distance using telecommunications technology."}, {"question": "What is a virus?", "options": ["A network protocol", "Malicious software that replicates itself and spreads to other computers", "A programming error", "A type of computer hardware"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "A computer virus is a type of malicious software that, when executed, repli  тcates itself by modifying other computer programs and inserting its own code."}, {"question": "What is spyware?", "options": ["Software that secretly monitors and collects user information", "A program for data encryption", "A type of security camera", "A tool for spying on people"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Spyware is software that enables a user to obtain covert information about another's computer activities by transmitting data covertly from their hard drive."}, {"question": "What do you wear in VR?", "options": ["A VR headset", "A helmet", "Special gloves", "A full-body suit"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "A VR headset is the primary device worn to experience virtual reality, providing visual and sometimes auditory immersion."}, {"question": "What is teamwork?", "options": ["Collaborative effort of a group to achieve a common goal", "Individual work", "Competition", "Delegation of tasks"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Teamwork involves individuals working together effectively to achieve shared objectives."}, {"question": "Software is a computer ___.", "options": ["hardware", "program", "network", "device"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Software refers to the programs and other operating information used by a computer."}, {"question": "What does malware do?", "options": ["Steal information", "Harm computer systems", "Disrupt operations", "All of the above"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Malware is a broad term for any software designed to cause damage, steal data, or disrupt computer operations."}, {"question": "What is a startup?", "options": ["A government agency", "A non-profit organization", "A large corporation", "A newly established business"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "A startup is a young company founded by one or more entrepreneurs to develop a unique product or service and bring it to market."}, {"question": "Do we ___ wear a uniform at your school?", "options": ["must", "should", "can", "have to"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"Do we have to\" is used to ask about an obligation or necessity."}, {"question": "I ___ wake up early on weekdays to catch the bus.", "options": ["should", "have to", "might", "can"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "\"Have to\" expresses a necessity or an obligation imposed by an external circumstance."}, {"question": "What is hacking?", "options": ["Playing video games", "Writing computer code", "Designing websites", "Gaining unauthorized access to computer systems"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Hacking refers to the act of identifying and exploiting weaknesses in computer systems or networks to gain unauthorized access."}, {"question": "What is a CV?", "options": ["A document summarizing a person's education, skills, and experience", "A type of computer virus", "A financial report", "A social media platform"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "A CV (Curriculum Vitae) is a detailed document outlining a person's academic and professional history."}, {"question": "What is ransomware?", "options": ["A type of antivirus software", "A network monitoring tool", "Malware that encrypts data and demands payment for its release", "A tool for data recovery"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Ransomware is a type of malware that encrypts a victim's files, blocking access until a ransom is paid."}, {"question": "What is entertainment technology?", "options": ["Technology for healthcare", "Technology for education", "Technology for business", "Technology used for leisure and amusement"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Entertainment technology encompasses devices and systems designed to provide enjoyment, such as gaming consoles, streaming services, and VR."}, {"question": "What can AI do?", "options": ["Learn", "Understand language", "Solve problems", "All of the above"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "AI systems are designed to perform various tasks that typically require human intelligence, such as learning, problem-solving, and natural language processing."}, {"question": "What do startups focus on?", "opt  уions": ["Large-scale manufacturing", "Maintaining existing products", "Innovation and rapid growth", "Government contracts"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Startups are typically new companies designed to grow fast by developing unique products or services."}, {"question": "What are hard skills?", "options": ["Measurable abilities learned through education or training", "Communication skills", "Personal attributes", "Teamwork abilities"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Hard skills are specific, teachable abilities that can be quantified, such as programming, data analysis, or foreign language proficiency."}, {"question": "What platform is commonly used for movies?", "options": ["LinkedIn", "Spotify", "Netflix", "Instagram"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Netflix is a popular streaming platform primarily known for its vast library of movies and TV shows."}, {"question": "Children ___ listen to their parents.", "options": ["might", "have to", "must", "should"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"Should\" is used for general advice or what is considered morally correct."}, {"question": "What do freelancers sell?", "options": ["Stocks and bonds", "Physical products", "Their skills and services", "Real estate"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Freelancers are self-employed individuals who offer their professional skills and services to clients on a project-by-project basis."}, {"question": "You ___ eat so much fast food. It's not healthy.", "options": ["shouldn't", "couldn't", "mustn't", "don't have to"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "\"Shouldn't\" is used to give advice or recommend against an action."}, {"question": "What is a 'Milestone'?", "options": ["A type of rock", "A significant point or stage in a project", "A measurement of distance", "A daily task"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "A milestone marks a specific, important point in a project's timeline, often indicating the completion of a major phase or deliverable."}, {"question": "Microsoft Word is ___ software.", "options": ["system", "programming", "utility", "application"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Microsoft Word is an application software used to perform specific tasks, in this case, word processing."}, {"question": "In a report, what is a 'Blocker'?", "options": ["A type of software", "An obstacle preventing progress", "A team member", "A project goal"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "A blocker is an issue or impediment that prevents a task or project from moving forward."}, {"question": "What is a Technical Demo?", "options": ["A presentation about project management", "A demonstration of a product's technical features and functionality", "A meeting to discuss technical problems", "A document outlining technical specifications"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "A technical demo showcases the practical application and capabilities of a product or system."}, {"question": "Why use antivirus?", "options": ["To detect and remove malware", "To speed up your computer", "To create documents", "To browse the internet faster"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Antivirus software is designed to prevent, detect, and remove malicious software like viruses, worms, and Trojans."}, {"question": "What is a strong password?", "options": ["Easy to remember", "A single word", "Your name or birthday", "Long, complex, and unique"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "A strong password typically includes a mix of uppercase and lowercase letters, numbers, and symbols, and is not easily guessable."}, {"question": "You ___ pay to enter the park. It is completely free.", "options": ["can't", "mustn't", "shouldn't", "don't have to"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"Don't have to\" indicates that something is not necessary or not an obligation."}, {"question": "What is Artificial Intelligence?", "options": ["A type of robot", "Machines that mimic human intelligence", "A computer game", "A new programming language"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "AI refers to the simulation of human intelligence in machines that ar  фe programmed to think like humans and mimic their actions."}, {"question": "What can AI recognize?", "options": ["Speech", "Faces", "Patterns", "All of the above"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "AI is capable of recognizing various forms of data, including faces, speech, and complex patterns."}, {"question": "What does K.I.S.S. mean?", "options": ["Keep It Secret, Safe", "Keep It Simple, Stupid", "Keep It Smart, Simple", "Keep It Short and Sweet"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "K.I.S.S. is an acronym for \"Keep It Simple, Stupid,\" a design principle that states that most systems work best if they are kept simple rather than made complicated."}, {"question": "Good UX means easy ___.", "options": ["to install", "to use", "to code", "to market"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "UX (User Experience) focuses on making a product enjoyable and easy for users to interact with."}, {"question": "What can you do in VR?", "options": ["Attend virtual meetings", "All of the above", "Play games", "Explore virtual worlds"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "VR offers a wide range of experiences, from immersive gaming and virtual tourism to educational simulations and collaborative workspaces."}, {"question": "Who writes code?", "options": ["Software developers", "Project managers", "Marketing specialists", "Graphic designers"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Software developers (or programmers) are responsible for writing, testing, and maintaining the source code of software programs."}, {"question": "What is Git used for?", "options": ["Version control", "Project management", "Graphic design", "Video editing"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Git is a distributed version control system used for tracking changes in source code during software development."}, {"question": "What is phishing?", "options": ["Tricking people into giving up sensitive information", "A network security device", "A computer game", "A type of fishing"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Phishing is a cybercrime where attackers disguise themselves as trustworthy entities to trick individuals into revealing sensitive information."}, {"question": "Which of these is a Voice Assistant?", "options": ["Microsoft Word", "Adobe Photoshop", "Siri", "Google Chrome"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Siri is Apple's virtual assistant that uses voice queries and a natural-language user interface to answer questions, make recommendations, and perform actions."}, {"question": "What is a Progress Report for?", "options": ["To report an incident", "To inform stakeholders about the status of a project", "To finalize a project", "To propose a new idea"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "A progress report provides an update on the status of a project or task, highlighting achievements, challenges, and next steps."}, {"question": "Who designs app look?", "options": ["Database administrators", "Software developers", "Network engineers", "UI/UX designers"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "UI (User Interface) designers focus on the visual and interactive elements of an app, determining its look and feel."}, {"question": "Google Docs is a ___ application.", "options": ["cloud-based", "mobile", "system", "desktop"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Google Docs operates entirely online through a web browser, making it a cloud-based application."}, {"question": "Which of these is an example of a programming language?", "options": ["Python", "Google Chrome", "Microsoft Word", "Photoshop"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Python is a widely used high-level programming language for general-purpose programming."}, {"question": "When do you write an Incident Report?", "options": ["To give a presentation", "After an unexpected event or accident", "To summarize daily tasks", "To plan a project"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "An incident report is a formal document that details the facts of an incident, accident, or near-miss."}, {"question": "What can you listen to on Spotify?", "options": ["Video games", "E-books", "Music and podcasts", "M    ovies"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Spotify is a digital music, podcast, and video service that gives you access to millions of songs and other content from creators all over the world."}, {"question": "What are soft skills?", "options": ["Technical expertise", "Financial management", "Project planning", "Personal attributes that enable effective interaction"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Soft skills are non-technical skills that relate to how you work and interact with others, such as communication, teamwork, and problem-solving."}, {"question": "User Interface (UI) means how software ___.", "options": ["stores information", "looks and interacts with users", "connects to the internet", "processes data"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "UI refers to the visual elements and interactive properties of a software that users interact with."}, {"question": "Students ___ bring a dictionary to the exam. It is not allowed.", "options": ["couldn't", "shouldn't", "don't have to", "mustn't"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "\"Mustn't\" indicates a strong prohibition or something that is not allowed."}, {"question": "What does a firewall do?", "options": ["Creates backups", "Stores data", "Speeds up internet connection", "Monitors and controls incoming and outgoing network traffic"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "A firewall acts as a barrier between a trusted internal network and untrusted external networks, controlling traffic based on security rules."}, {"question": "What is a 'Summary'?", "options": ["A personal opinion", "A detailed analysis", "A list of all facts", "A brief statement of the main points"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "A summary provides a concise overview of the key information or main ideas of a longer text or presentation."}, {"question": "What is streaming?", "options": ["Storing data on a hard drive", "Sending emails", "Delivering media content over the internet in real-time", "Downloading files"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Streaming allows users to consume media content (audio or video) as it is being delivered, without needing to download the entire file first."}, {"question": "What do PC games use?", "options": ["A gaming console", "A smartphone", "A computer and monitor", "A VR headset"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "PC games are played on personal computers, typically requiring a monitor, keyboard, and mouse."}, {"question": "Google Drive is a type of cloud ___.", "options": ["computing", "security", "networking", "storage"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Google Drive is a file storage and synchronization service developed by Google, allowing users to store files on their servers."}, {"question": "What is data?", "options": ["A type of computer virus", "Facts and statistics collected together for reference or analysis", "A hardware component", "A programming language"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Data refers to raw facts, figures, or information that can be processed or stored by a computer."}, {"question": "Microsoft Azure is a cloud ___.", "options": ["platform", "operating system", "application", "device"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Microsoft Azure is a comprehensive set of cloud services that developers and IT professionals use to build, deploy, and manage applications through a global network of Microsoft-managed data centers. It's a cloud computing platform."}, {"question": "What does 'Proofread' mean?", "options": ["To write a draft", "To read and correct errors in text", "To publish a document", "To summarize a text"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Proofreading involves carefully checking a text for grammatical, spelling, punctuation, and formatting errors before final submission."}, {"question": "Who are 'Non-technical' people?", "options": ["Software developers", "Engineers", "IT support staff", "Individuals without specialized knowledge in a technical field"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Non-technical people are those who do not have expertise or a deep understanding of technical subjects."}]}j™0
