n email", "To write a draft"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Proofreading is the process of reading text to identify and correct errors in grammar, spelling, and punctuation."}, {"question": "What does K.I.S.S. mean?", "options": ["Kindly Inform Senior Staff", "Know Important Syst  Aem Secrets", "Keep It Simple, Stupid", "Keep It Safe and Secure"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "K.I.S.S. is a design principle that advocates for simplicity in design and avoiding unnecessary complexity."}, {"question": "Example of programming language?", "options": ["Google Chrome", "Photoshop", "Microsoft Word", "Python"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Python is a widely used high-level programming language."}, {"question": "When do you write an Incident Report?", "options": ["To summarize daily tasks", "To request vacation", "After an unexpected event or accident", "Before starting a project"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Incident reports are documented after an unusual or adverse event to record details and aid in analysis."}, {"question": "He has a bad cold. He ___ stay in bed today.", "options": ["must", "might", "has to", "should"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "This is advice for someone who is unwell."}, {"question": "System software example is ___.", "options": ["Photoshop", "Microsoft Word", "Windows", "Google Chrome"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Windows is an operating system, which is a type of system software."}, {"question": "Why use antivirus?", "options": ["To speed up your computer", "To browse the internet safely", "To store files", "To protect against viruses and malware"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Antivirus software scans for, detects, and removes malicious software like viruses and other malware."}, {"question": "What does malware do?", "options": ["Connects to the internet", "Speeds up computers", "Harms computer systems", "Protects data"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Malware is software designed to cause damage, disrupt operations, or gain unauthorized access to computer systems."}, {"question": "What can you listen to on Spotify?", "options": ["Music and podcasts", "E-books", "Video games", "Movies"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "Spotify is an audio streaming platform offering a wide range of music and podcasts."}, {"question": "What does cybersecurity protect?", "options": ["Financial investments", "Human health", "Physical buildings", "Digital data and systems"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Cybersecurity is about protecting information and systems from unauthorized access or damage."}, {"question": "What are hard skills?", "options": ["Communication skills", "Teamwork abilities", "Personal qualities", "Teachable and measurable abilities"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Hard skills are specific, quantifiable abilities that can be taught and measured, such as programming or data analysis."}, {"question": "What is Git used for?", "options": ["Graphic design", "Data storage", "Version control", "Project management"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "Git is a distributed version control system used for tracking changes in source code during software development."}, {"question": "What is a startup?", "options": ["A government agency", "A newly established business", "A large corporation", "A non-profit organization"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "A startup is a newly established business, often technology-driven, with the aim of rapid growth."}, {"question": "What is phishing?", "options": ["A type of computer game", "A method of coding", "A way to browse the internet", "Tricking people into giving personal information"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "Phishing uses deceptive emails or websites to trick users into revealing sensitive data like passwords or credit card numbers."}, {"question": "What are soft skills?", "options": ["Technical knowledge", "Personal attributes and interpersonal skills", "Programming languages", "Data analysis"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Soft skills are personal attributes that enable effective interaction with others, such as communication and teamwork."}, {"question": "Which of these is a Voice Assistant?", "options": ["Photoshop", "Siri", "Google Chrome", "Microsoft Word"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Siri is Apple's virtual assistant that uses voice recogni    tion to perform tasks."}, {"question": "What can you do in VR?", "options": ["Write documents", "Make phone calls", "Play games and explore virtual worlds", "Send emails"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "VR allows users to interact with and explore simulated environments, often for gaming or educational purposes."}, {"question": "What can AI do?", "options": ["Cook food", "Build houses", "Learn and solve problems", "Drive cars manually"], "correct_index": 2, "explanation": "AI is designed to process information, learn from it, and make decisions or solve problems."}, {"question": "What does a firewall do?", "options": ["Stores data", "Blocks unauthorized access to a network", "Creates backups", "Speeds up internet connection"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "A firewall acts as a barrier between a trusted internal network and untrusted external networks, controlling traffic."}, {"question": "User Interface (UI) means how software ___.", "options": ["looks", "is coded", "functions", "stores data"], "correct_index": 0, "explanation": "UI focuses on the visual elements and interactive parts of a software that users see and interact with."}, {"question": "I ___ wake up early on weekdays to catch the bus.", "options": ["should", "can", "must", "have to"], "correct_index": 3, "explanation": "This expresses an external obligation or necessity."}, {"question": "What is spyware?", "options": ["A network monitoring device", "Software that secretly collects information", "A tool for system optimization", "A type of operating system"], "correct_index": 1, "explanation": "Spyware is softwar